From 0bebc403ff1e9ae535f2eb41744abd9aa80d22b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:13:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(kanban): pin case-insensitive relative .HERMES/ hit
 naming in _state_path [daveey]

Post-merge mutation check of PR #2533 (card t_01a1d6672f6410cf) found
survivor F7: dropping re.IGNORECASE from _REL_STATE in
hermes_cli/kanban_home_marker_placement.py left both state-path test
files green. The state-path rule matches case-insensitively, so
`cd ~ && cat .HERMES/logs/x.log` is a hit; without the flag
_REL_STATE.match returns None and the hit falls back to the whole
`cd ~ && cat .HERMES/...` span instead of `~/.HERMES/logs/x.log`.

Test-only: adds an upper-case row to
test_relative_state_path_hit_is_the_home_path_not_the_cd_span.

Proof (hermes-worker-1, base origin/main 987876f5d0):
- GREEN: scripts/run_tests.sh tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_state_path_home_forms.py
  tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pool_queue.py -> 171 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped
- RED under F7: same command -> 170 passed, 1 failed (the new row:
  hit 'cd ~ && cat .HERMES/l...' != '~/.HERMES/logs/x.log')

The row uses a logs path (class b) rather than a workspace path: _ARTIFACT
is case-sensitive, so ~/.HERMES/kanban/workspaces/... classifies as b, and
this row pins only the hit naming F7 breaks.
---
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_state_path_home_forms.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_state_path_home_forms.py b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_state_path_home_forms.py
index 29bd644b3f..32261182b7 100644
--- a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_state_path_home_forms.py
+++ b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_state_path_home_forms.py
@@ -124,6 +124,8 @@ def test_many_cd_home_lines_without_a_state_path_scan_in_linear_time():
     # PR #2533 review: ``"\u0130".lower()`` is two code points, so an offset taken on the lowered span shifted.
     ("cd ~ && make all \u0130 && cat .hermes/kanban/workspaces/t_x/f", "artifact-not-here",
      "~/.hermes/kanban/workspaces/t_x/f"),
+    # The state-path rule is case-insensitive, so an upper-case relative path is still named as its ``~/`` path.
+    ("cd ~ && cat .HERMES/logs/x.log", "b", "~/.HERMES/logs/x.log"),
 ])
 def test_relative_state_path_hit_is_the_home_path_not_the_cd_span(body, cls, path, tmp_path, monkeypatch):
     from hermes_cli import kanban_home_marker_placement as hm
